$( <MM> <PROOF_ASST> THEOREM=rectintana  LOC_AFTER=?

* A holomorphic function on a rectangle is analytic: its Taylor partial sums about a strictly interior centre P converge to 2 pi i times its value at every strictly interior point Z within half the distance R from P to the boundary frame.

